WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:06.000
Everyone knows Batman as one of the flagship DC&nbsp;
Comics characters. The Dark Knight himself has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.480
consistently ranked as one of the world's&nbsp;
most popular superheroes, rivaling -- and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:14.880
often completely outperforming -- most of the&nbsp;
major figures of the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:16.160
"Who the hell are you supposed to be?"

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:28.160
As such, Bats often becomes part of a much&nbsp;
larger rivalry between two comic book giants,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:31.520
but it's worth noting that this&nbsp;
conflict exists more in the heads&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:35.280
of fans than it does behind the&nbsp;
scenes -- where actors, creators,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:40.000
and other talent often feel free to hop&nbsp;
between the DC and Marvel universes with ease.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.400
For instance, the upcoming Warner Bros&nbsp;
film "The Batman," which reimagines the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:49.120
Gotham City legend in an even darker light&nbsp;
than before, contains a number of actors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:54.160
you will recognize. In fact, while you might&nbsp;
not realize it at first, three major actors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:59.040
from the Marvel Cinematic Universe will be&nbsp;
shifting their gaze over to DC in this film.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:03.040
The first of Marvel's movie-hopping&nbsp;
mega-stars actually didn't appear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:08.080
until midway through the "Infinity Saga,"&nbsp;
and that's former Gollum actor Andy Serkis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:13.360
who is the newest actor to portray Bruce Wayne's&nbsp;
butler, Alfred Pennyworth in "The Batman."

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:17.920
In the MCU, Serkis' character is a&nbsp;
lot more villainous, as he played&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:23.200
Ulysses Klaue . Originally appearing in "Avengers:&nbsp;
Age of Ultron" before making his way into "Black&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:29.360
Panther," Klaue is the underground arms dealer&nbsp;
responsible for stealing vibranium from Wakanda.

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:33.760
While initially framed as the primary&nbsp;
antagonist of "Black Panther," a plot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:38.800
twist sees him murdered by his associate,&nbsp;
Erik Killmonger, who betrays Klaue as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:43.920
means of entering Wakanda so that he may&nbsp;
challenge T'Challa and overthrow his rule.

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:48.160
The MCU isn't the only Marvel movie&nbsp;
property that Serkis is tied to.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:51.760
He was also the director of "Venom:&nbsp;
Let There Be Carnage." As such,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:57.600
he is the only actor on this list that has&nbsp;
direct connections to both DC and the MCU,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:02.160
while also having a role to play in Sony's&nbsp;
line of "Spider-Man"-adjacent films.

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:07.920
Along with Serkis, Irish actor Barry Keoghan&nbsp;
also appears in both "The Batman" and the MCU,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:11.280
though his entry into the latter&nbsp;
occurred much later than that of Serkis.

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:15.360
Keoghan is in "The Batman" as a&nbsp;
character who was kept secret.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:19.360
Officially billed in pre-release&nbsp;
materials as "Officer Stanley Merkel,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:23.360
the character he actually plays in&nbsp;
the movie is much more mysterious.

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:27.680
We do know for certain that his MCU&nbsp;
character, the Eternal known as Druig,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:33.200
is poised to continue appearing in future films.&nbsp;
In "Eternals," Druig -- with his power of mind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:38.480
control -- becomes one of the few Eternals to&nbsp;
rebel against his Celestial creators, though it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:43.040
remains to be seen how he and his surviving&nbsp;
family may be punished for their rebellion.

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:48.320
Finally, when it comes to joint actors shared&nbsp;
between the MCU and "The Batman," there is Jeffrey&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:53.840
Wright, who plays the famous James Gordon in the&nbsp;
latter. In most Batman stories, James Gordon is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:59.520
well known as the Gotham City Police Commissioner&nbsp;
and father of Barbara Gordon, aka Batgirl.

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:05.920
He is one of Batman's closest and most trustworthy&nbsp;
collaborators, and the main reason why the GCPD&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:11.760
is often depicted as having a working relationship&nbsp;
with the Bat. Gordon is an instantly recognizable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:17.280
role, to be sure, most famously embodied in past&nbsp;
films by Gary Oldman in the "Dark Knight" trilogy.

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:22.240
On the MCU side of things, however, Wright's&nbsp;
role is deceptively difficult to pick out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:26.800
if you don't pay attention. That's because&nbsp;
unlike the other actors listed, Wright's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:32.320
role in the MCU is entirely done by voice, and&nbsp;
he (so far) has not appeared in any movies.

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:36.960
"This mission requires a team with the&nbsp;
perfect combination of skills and experience."

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:42.320
Instead, Wright's character of Uatu,&nbsp;
aka the Watcher -- a cosmic being that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:47.040
observes events across the multiverse --&nbsp;
only occurs in the animated Disney+ series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:50.240
"What If...?" Despite Uatu's&nbsp;
efforts to remain impartial,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:55.040
the series shows him eventually realizing that&nbsp;
a growing threat requires his intervention.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:04:00.160
With "The Batman," however, we will finally see&nbsp;
Wright in a mainline, live-action comic book film.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:04.720
It's an exciting step to see the actor take,&nbsp;
since Wright has been impressing critics since his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:11.040
breakout role in "Basquiat" back in 1996 … also&nbsp;
starring another Commissioner Gordon, Gary Oldman.

